  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef is preparing to cook his dinner.\n\nThere are two dishes Chef can make. The first one contains F1F_1F1​ grams of fat and P1P_1P1​ grams of protein, while the second contains F2F_2F2​ grams of fat and P2P_2P2​ grams of protein.\n\nChef would like the quantity of fats and proteins he consumes to be as close to each other as possible, i.e., the absolute difference between the amount of fats and proteins should be as small as possible.\n\nHelp Chef by telling him which dish he'll choose; or if both dishes have the same difference.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains four space-separated integers F1,P1,F2,F_1, P_1, F_2,F1​,P1​,F2​, and P2P_2P2​ — the quantities of fat and protein in the first dish and second dish, respectively.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single string:\n\n\n\n`\"First\"` (without quotes) if Chef will choose the first dish.\n`\"Second\"` (without quotes) if Chef will choose the second dish.\n`\"Both\"` (without quotes) if both dishes are equivalent.\n\nEach character of the output may be in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e. if the answer is `Both`, then any of the strings `BOTH`, `both`, `Both`, `bOTh`, and so on will be accepted.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤F1,P1,F2,P2≤1001 \\leq F_1, P_1, F_2, P_2 \\leq 1001≤F1​,P1​,F2​,P2​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "30 40 35 44",
        "output": "Second",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe first dish has a difference of ∣30−40∣=10|30 - 40| = 10∣30−40∣=10 between its fats and proteins, while the second dish has a difference of ∣35−44∣=9|35 - 44| = 9∣35−44∣=9.\nChef will choose the second dish, since it has a smaller difference."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1 100 100 1",
        "output": "Both",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe first dish has a difference of ∣1−100∣=99|1 - 100| = 99∣1−100∣=99 between its fats and proteins, while the second dish has a difference of ∣100−1∣=99|100 - 1| = 99∣100−1∣=99.\nBoth dishes have the same difference."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "58 56 38 52",
        "output": "First",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe first dish has a difference of ∣58−56∣=2|58 - 56| = 2∣58−56∣=2 between its fats and proteins, while the second dish has a difference of ∣38−52∣=14|38 - 52| = 14∣38−52∣=14.\nChef will choose the first dish, since it has a smaller difference."
      }
    ]
  },
